[Music]  this morning on the dish we take you to  england to meet a chef reviving a  british classic the savory pie  column franklin with his team at  london's holborn dining room at the  rosewood hotel craft phenomenal  creations designed to please both the  palette and the eye mts taeyab went to  meet the city's undisputed king of pies  behind these doors  is where british pie making is at its  most refined  chef callum franklin of the holborn  dining room located in the heart of  central london takes the crafting of the  traditional savory typically meat-filled  and pastry-wrapped parcels to a whole  new level  was any part of you worried about  i don't know if londoners want to eat  pies no  the native south londoner designed the  restaurant's pie room himself and filled  it with antique copper pie molds dating  back to the victorian era  celebrating a national food culture that  was first recorded over 600 years ago  and is still beloved by home cooks today  and actually so subconsciously it  transports you back to your family table  right simpler times  sat you know  getting abused from your brother and  sister at a dinner table it's an  a nice link to that part of your  childhood and we do that  whilst making it very elegant as well  did you need a room for it though 100  with the peak of its popularity during  the victorian era pies were fuel mainly  for the poor who could fill their  bellies for little more than a penny  nearly a century later pie and mass  shops remained a staple in working class  areas of south and east london but today  the traditional eateries are on the  brink of extinction a food history  franklin is trying to save  along with his number two knox majosi a  south african-born londoner who has  earned the title of master pie maker  growing up in south africa did you ever  think you'd be in a room like this in  london making pies  not at all  what does it make you feel when people  call you a master pie maker for me i  find like you know what for me this at  the end i find what i love the most it's  fills me with joy that you know what i'm  doing what i love now at the hoben  dining room the pies may cost a little  bit more than a penny but come filled  with carefully sourced ingredients like  the classic pork pie which is made of  hand raised pork shoulder smoked bacon  fennel seed and sage or the decidedly  french-inspired dolphinwa potato pie  made with winterdale english cheddar and  caramelized onion  all hand crafted and resembling edible  art images of which that have gone viral  thanks to franklin's wildly popular  instagram page  it was my wife who said to me you know  you should you should put something on  instagram you know this work you're  doing people are going to be interested  in  and i was like no one's going to be  interested in brown food  brown pies on instagram yeah and we  started to post stuff  and it just went wild  franklin who is toiled in some of  britain's finest kitchens knows a thing  or two about living the wildlife for the  first decade of his career he was in his  own words an alcoholic  your relationship with alcohol  became kind of a problem didn't they  yeah definitely so i went into rehab in  the end you know i how old are you  so i was  30.  drinking so much every day  and on the job he says he physically  couldn't stop  and in the end yeah it just  sort of primal instinct kind of must  have kicked in and one day i reached out  to my brother and said  i need help i need to go to rehab today  because i think i knew i was going to  die  and uh  he just said you know we've been waiting  for you to say this for  so so long  for franklin the savory pie soon became  something of a savior a taste from his  childhood he could elevate and perfect  for his diners  and then there's some chicken pie  chicken and  chestnut mushroom pie  classic british pie biggest seller on  the menu lots of peas  and some chicken gravy it's just  one of those flavors  right that you've just had your whole  life and yeah it's like a blanket yeah  and the crab thermador wrapped in pastry  i mean this  tastes like the sea  the one thing i should say is the pastry  so flaky  so good and so light as well that's  knoxy working  such supercharged flavors aren't always  associated with traditional british  cookery something franklin says he's  acutely aware of  as someone who thinks so deeply about  what you put on these plates every  single day  what do you want to do next  so really i would love to do this  but on a larger scale  and raise the whole pie game in the uk  so it really becomes back to being  something celebratory you know something  we all get behind and people are proud  of for cbs saturday morning empty house  time  london  that was good oh my gosh come to new  york with those works  that's why they're not here by the way  because they're so delicate and so  beautiful  you can't get them that far yeah saved  us on the diet right it did but that  would be awful and look good yeah  incredible

